**Definition 16.1 (installation, source adapter and service costs).** Let
$m_L=|E(L)|,m_1=|E(D_1)|$ be the actual native installation bit lengths,
and let $d_1=|\Delta(D_1)|$ be the archival description-frame payload length.
All include their displayed finite initial control/token data. They are computable lengths
of the two specified expansions, including ManifestPrefix's actual entry,
tests and word helpers, not interpreter constants. Their canonical supplied
code words and all later replay counts use this same expansion. Installation's
vector consists of one activation CTL; the two ordinary bitwise bootstraps,
$4(m_L+m_1)+4$ for their tested NEXT, IN, one-bit constructor-WR,
ADVANCE and final DONE rows, with no ordinary boundary construction;
$L$'s eight actual port-token TOKs, the one receiver-port handoff TOK and its entire paid
code-frame acquisition/descriptor/seal; its return-to-bootstrap CTL;
and the actual source-head saves/restores, sentinel appends, asset copies,
$j_A$ scan, manifest framing/seals, bank initialization and final token/
Ready steps. For each item use Definition 11.5 and the explicitly specified
copy/ingress schemata. Existing ordinary boundary cells are not constructed
again. New finite control bits contribute their actual encoded bit count
to $b_{\rm ctl}$; they are not eight-bit ordinary cells. The captured code
frame's ingress, length and descriptor work is additional to both control
bootstraps. Its Import runs only after $D_1$ is installed.

Full manifest import is exactly Definition 13.2's ManifestPrefix, entered
after the native empty-bank construction. Its native scan vector is
Lemma 13.2a's, with scalar $2h+4+3s+3z+4o$ at the actual head distance
and actual field values. Add that lemma's ordered word-instruction list
with Definition 11.5's recurrence at every actual successor. The two
entrance MRs each have their own receipt/tick/fee; no F is imported for
the sentinel, and every empty field still incurs BeginField, clear,
terminator, Reverse, AppendItem and move work. The field-zero tag/length/
payload/exhaustion checks, row validation and old-list parsing then use
their explicit word expansions. These are installation-purpose work,
not free admission, a receipt-position readout or service-frame ingress.
Its source descriptors are preserved; new bank descriptors and retained
versions are additional storage and cost. This is a full recurrence for
this graph, rather than a constant correction to another graph's total:
the acquired and installed code lengths themselves are lengths of this
expansion. Later Boundary and Prefix likewise count its actual rows.

The ingress price includes its actual admission TOK, reserve CTL, Base
and descriptor recipe. Its three
headers contribute 12 occurrences, its $d+1$ length bits contribute
$5(d+1)$, its payload loop contributes $6d+1$, and its F/seal contributes
4. This subtotal is $11d+22$, before admission TOK, reserve, Base, length copy, all
scratch positioning/seals, $U(2d+4)$ construction, descriptor and Import.
The acquired frame has $2d+4$ actual INs. Import is its complete native
RD/test, cons-bank assignment and MR loop plus final Reverse; it is
not included in that subtotal.

Every original source-frame IN replaced after activation contributes an
actual RD and MR instead; count the resulting original graph word and
all its unchanged original source/body rows on this run. The adapter
has no IN of its own and does not charge the earlier physical ingress
twice. Original boot/acquisition, old finite completion and activation
are distinct actual fragments. No discarded AIF offset is revived.

For a word instruction and a service handler, use Definition 11.5's
recurrence on its finite expanded word program. Thus the costs of
row lookup, full cell scans, list replacement, code/latch/token update,
receipt/event serialization, countdown tests, all scratch and descriptor
records and all bank copies are included. Boundary's loop uses its
actual represented Ready/frame/activation tests; Prefix's loop uses its
constructed countdown. Its physical cost generally exceeds the number
of represented primitives by an unbounded factor.

Archive output uses the Base/dry-count/copy/descriptor recipe of
Definition 13.4. For each initialized mailbox or receiver, add its full
Base, actual length preparation, complete Allocate including its single
delimiter, descriptor and positioning recipe. Its six-row copy then
contributes $6l+3$; together the two bodies are $12l+6$. These body
formulas do not include the initialized copies' setup, lengths, descriptors,
repositioning, the two sealed completion-record constructions of Definition
13.2, or the mandatory $5l+1$ RD/OUT print loop and its fresh length
recovery/positioning. The finite token admission,
acknowledgement, purpose transitions and Ready return are their actual
TOK/CTL occurrences, in addition to body handoffs already counted.

